[dvystrcil/homelab] Add monthly restic restore test for claude memory backup  (model=qwen3-coder-next:latest, 35s, lane=claude)
## Why
The claude memory is backed up via restic to TrueNAS, but there is no verification that restores actually work. A backup without tested restores is not a backup — it only confirms data *was* present at backup time, not that it can be recovered when needed.

## What we know
- claude memory is stored in `claude-personal-config` and backed up via restic to TrueNAS (per architecture docs and repo READMEs).
- The homelab already has restic workflows (e.g., `bin/restic-backup.sh`, `bin/restic-prune.sh`) and TrueNAS replication patterns documented in `homelab/architecture/`.
- Issue https://github.com/dvystrcil/homelab/issues/29 (disaster recovery playbook) is open and covers backup/restore verification, but does not specify automated monthly restore tests for individual datasets like claude memory.

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] **AC1.** A scheduled workflow (`bin/test-restic-restore.sh`) runs monthly, restores the latest claude memory snapshot to a temp directory, verifies integrity, and deletes the temp directory.
- [ ] **AC2.** The workflow fails the run if the restore or integrity check fails (non-zero exit code).
- [ ] **AC3.** The workflow sends a Slack notification on failure (reuse existing `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` pattern from other workflows).

## Lane
claude — requires design of the restore test script, integration with existing restic tooling, and scheduling in the homelab's CI/CD (cron workflow). Touches multiple repos: homelab (script + cron), claude-personal-config (backup path definition), and potentially cluster-ops if TrueNAS credentials are involved.

